## Relevant FTXUI APIs and monochrome patterns

FTXUI’s usable “no explicit color” toolbox for compare panes is mostly: `Table`, `hbox`/`vbox`, `separator*`, `border*`/`window`, `gauge*`, `graph`, `size`, `flex`/`xflex`, `frame`, and alignment decorators.

### 1. Tables for structured comparisons

**Claim**: Use `ftxui::Table` when columns must align across rows; it supports selecting rows/columns/cells, adding borders/separators, and decorating cells independently.

**Evidence** ([table.hpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/include/ftxui/dom/table.hpp#L16-L53)):

```cpp
/// @brief Table is a utility to draw tables.
class FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Table {
 public:
  Table();
  explicit Table(const std::vector<std::vector<std::string>>&);
  explicit Table(std::vector<std::vector<Element>>);
  Table(std::initializer_list<std::vector<std::string>> init);
  TableSelection SelectAll();
  TableSelection SelectCell(int column, int row);
  TableSelection SelectRow(int row_index);
  TableSelection SelectRows(int row_min, int row_max);
  TableSelection SelectColumn(int column_index);
  TableSelection SelectColumns(int column_min, int column_max);
  TableSelection SelectRectangle(int column_min,
                                 int column_max,
                                 int row_min,
                                 int row_max);
  Element Render();
```

**Pattern**: Official example creates the table, adds a global light border, adds stronger header borders/separators, right-aligns a column, and renders with `Dimension::Fit`.

**Evidence** ([examples/dom/table.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/examples/dom/table.cpp#L17-L64)):

```cpp
auto table = Table({
    {"Version", "Marketing name", "Release date", "API level", "Runtime"},
    {"2.3", "Gingerbread", "February 9 2011", "10", "Dalvik 1.4.0"},
    // ...
});

table.SelectAll().Border(LIGHT);

// Add border around the first column.
table.SelectColumn(0).Border(LIGHT);

// Make first row bold with a double border.
table.SelectRow(0).Decorate(bold);
table.SelectRow(0).SeparatorVertical(LIGHT);
table.SelectRow(0).Border(DOUBLE);

// Align right the "Release date" column.
table.SelectColumn(2).DecorateCells(align_right);

auto document = table.Render();
auto screen =
    Screen::Create(Dimension::Fit(document, /*extend_beyond_screen=*/true));
```

**No-color recommendation**: Replace color-coded alternate rows with `bold`, `dim`, `Border(DOUBLE)`, `SeparatorVertical(LIGHT/HEAVY/DOUBLE)`, and `align_right`. Avoid `DecorateCellsAlternateRow(color(...))` from the official example.

**Caveat**: `Table::Render()` transforms the table into a `gridbox` and resets internal dimensions, so treat a `Table` as render-once per frame/model state, not as a reusable rendered object.

**Evidence** ([src/ftxui/dom/table.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/table.cpp#L206-L230)):

```cpp
Element Table::Render() {
  for (int y = 0; y < dim_y_; ++y) {
    for (int x = 0; x < dim_x_; ++x) {
      auto& it = elements_[y][x];

      // Line
      if ((x + y) % 2 == 1) {
        it = std::move(it) | flex;
        continue;
      }

      // Cells
      if ((x % 2) == 1 && (y % 2) == 1) {
        it = std::move(it) | flex_shrink;
        continue;
      }

      // Corners
      it = std::move(it) | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, 0) | size(HEIGHT, EQUAL, 0);
    }
  }
  dim_x_ = 0;
  dim_y_ = 0;
  return gridbox(std::move(elements_));
}
```

