### 2. Gauges/progress bars for scalar comparisons

**Claim**: `gauge`, `gaugeLeft`, `gaugeRight`, `gaugeUp`, `gaugeDown`, and `gaugeDirection` are official DOM elements and do not require colors.

**Evidence** ([elements.hpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/include/ftxui/dom/elements.hpp#L77-L82)):

```cpp
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gauge(float progress);
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gaugeLeft(float progress);
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gaugeRight(float progress);
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gaugeUp(float progress);
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gaugeDown(float progress);
FTXUI_EXPORT(DOM) Element gaugeDirection(float progress, Direction direction);
```

**Claim**: Gauge values are clamped to `[0, 1]`, including NaN handling, so compare bars should normalize values before passing them in but are protected from over/underflow display.

**Evidence** ([src/ftxui/dom/gauge.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/gauge.cpp#L47-L56)):

```cpp
Gauge(float progress, Direction direction)
    : progress_(progress), direction_(direction) {
  // This handle NAN correctly:
  if (!(progress_ > 0.F)) {
    progress_ = 0.F;
  }
  if (!(progress_ < 1.F)) {
    progress_ = 1.F;
  }
}
```

**Pattern**: For “bar chart” style rows, combine fixed-width label/value cells with `separator()` and `gauge(ratio)`. The package-manager example is already a text + gauge row pattern.

**Evidence** ([examples/dom/package_manager.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/examples/dom/package_manager.cpp#L51-L65)):

```cpp
auto to_text = [](int number) {
  return text(std::to_string(number)) | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, 3);
};

auto renderTask = [&](const Task& task) {
  auto style = (task.downloaded == task.size) ? dim : bold;
  return hbox({
      text(task.name) | style,
      separator(),
      to_text(task.downloaded),
      text("/"),
      to_text(task.size),
      separator(),
      gauge(task.downloaded / float(task.size)),
  });
};
```

**No-color recommendation**: For compare rows, use:

```cpp
hbox({
  text(label) | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, 18),
  separator(),
  gauge(normalized) | flex,
  separator(),
  text(value) | align_right | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, 8),
});
```

Use `bold` for selected/important rows and `dim` for inactive/equal rows; do not use `color()`.

**Caveat**: Gauge rendering uses block characters and has terminal-specific fallback behavior.

**Evidence** ([src/ftxui/dom/gauge.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/gauge.cpp#L93-L98)):

```cpp
