**Claim**: `GraphFunction` is `std::function<std::vector<int>(int, int)>`, meaning the graph renderer asks your data function for a vector based on current render width/height.

**Evidence** ([elements.hpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/include/ftxui/dom/elements.hpp#L21-L25)):

```cpp
using Element = std::shared_ptr<Node>;
using Elements = std::vector<Element>;
using Decorator = std::function<Element(Element)>;
using GraphFunction = std::function<std::vector<int>(int, int)>;
```

**Pattern**: Official graph example places multiple graphs in `hbox`/`vbox`, separated with `separator()`, and uses `flex`.

**Evidence** ([examples/dom/graph.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/examples/dom/graph.cpp#L53-L69)):

```cpp
auto document = hbox({
    vbox({
        graph(std::ref(my_graph)),
        separator(),
        graph(triangle) | inverted,
    }) | flex,
    separator(),
    vbox({
        graph(std::ref(my_graph)) | color(Color::BlueLight),
        separator(),
        graph(std::ref(my_graph)) | color(Color::RedLight),
        separator(),
        graph(std::ref(my_graph)) | color(Color::YellowLight),
    }) | flex,
});

document |= border;
```

**No-color recommendation**: Use the left half of this pattern: plain `graph(...)`, separators, borders, optional `inverted` only if acceptable. Since your colors are configured globally later, omit `color(Color::...)`.

**Caveat**: `graph` has a minimum requirement of `3x3` and grows/shrinks in both axes, so it is suitable for flexible panes but needs enough height to be meaningful.

**Evidence** ([src/ftxui/dom/graph.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/graph.cpp#L35-L42)):

```cpp
void ComputeRequirement() override {
  requirement_.flex_grow_x = 1;
  requirement_.flex_grow_y = 1;
  requirement_.flex_shrink_x = 1;
  requirement_.flex_shrink_y = 1;
  requirement_.min_x = 3;
  requirement_.min_y = 3;
}
```

**Caveat**: The graph renderer doubles the logical resolution: it computes `width = cell_width * 2` and `height = cell_height * 2`, then calls your `GraphFunction(width, height)`. Your function must return enough data for that width.

**Evidence** ([src/ftxui/dom/graph.cpp](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/graph.cpp#L44-L61)):

```cpp
const int width = (box_.x_max - box_.x_min + 1) * 2;
const int height = (box_.y_max - box_.y_min + 1) * 2;
if (width <= 0 || height <= 0) {
  return;
}

auto data = graph_function_(width, height);
int i = 0;
for (int x = box_.x_min; x <= box_.x_max; ++x) {
  const int height_1 = 2 * box_.y_max - data.at(static_cast<size_t>(i++));
  const int height_2 = 2 * box_.y_max - data.at(static_cast<size_t>(i++));
