### 1. `hbox` allocates width from each child’s `Requirement::min_x`, then distributes leftover only to flex-grow children

**Claim:** In an `hbox`, fixed-width/non-flex children keep their required width; extra terminal columns go only to children whose requirement has `flex_grow_x != 0`. If nothing before/right of the panel grows appropriately, leftover appears as blank space.

**Evidence** ([source](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/hbox.cpp#L24-L40)):

```cpp
void ComputeRequirement() override {
  requirement_ = Requirement{};

  for (auto& child : children_) {
    child->ComputeRequirement();

    // Extend the min_x and min_y to contain all the children
    requirement_.min_x += child->requirement().min_x;
    requirement_.min_y =
        std::max(requirement_.min_y, child->requirement().min_y);
  }
}
```

**Evidence** ([source](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/hbox.cpp#L43-L63)):

```cpp
void SetBox(Box box) override {
  Node::SetBox(box);

  std::vector<box_helper::Element> elements(children_.size());
  for (size_t i = 0; i < children_.size(); ++i) {
    auto& element = elements[i];
    const auto& requirement = children_[i]->requirement();
    element.min_size = requirement.min_x;
    element.flex_grow = requirement.flex_grow_x;
    element.flex_shrink = requirement.flex_shrink_x;
  }
  const int target_size = box.x_max - box.x_min + 1;
  box_helper::Compute(&elements, target_size);

  int x = box.x_min;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < children_.size(); ++i) {
    box.x_min = x;
    box.x_max = x + elements[i].size - 1;
    children_[i]->SetBox(box);
    x = box.x_max + 1;
  }
}
```

**Evidence** ([source](https://github.com/ArthurSonzogni/FTXUI/blob/a9ddb312f9b00dd492ba73b5394a72c601ef2c94/src/ftxui/dom/box_helper.cpp#L74-L99)):

```cpp
void Compute(std::vector<Element>* elements, int target_size) {
  int size = 0;
  int flex_grow_sum = 0;
  int flex_shrink_sum = 0;
  int flex_shrink_size = 0;

  for (auto& element : *elements) {
    flex_grow_sum += element.flex_grow;
    flex_shrink_sum += element.min_size * element.flex_shrink;
    if (element.flex_shrink != 0) {
      flex_shrink_size += element.min_size;
    }
    size += element.min_size;
  }

  const int extra_space = target_size - size;
  if (extra_space >= 0) {
    ComputeGrow(elements, extra_space, flex_grow_sum);
  } else if (flex_shrink_size + extra_space >= 0) {
    ComputeShrinkEasy(elements, extra_space, flex_shrink_sum);
  } else {
    ComputeShrinkHard(elements, extra_space + flex_shrink_size,
                      size - flex_shrink_size);
  }
}
```

**Implication:** A two-pane layout like:

```cpp
hbox({
  left,
  right | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, width),
})
```

will not necessarily place the right panel against the terminal’s far-right edge. If total required width is less than the screen and no earlier child/filler absorbs the extra space, the blank columns are after the right panel.

