## Most likely cause of the small right-edge gap

The most likely cause is one of these:

### Cause A — the right detail panel is fixed-width, so it is not consuming leftover columns

If you have:

```cpp
hbox({
  left,
  right | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width),
})
```

then the right panel’s whole width is exactly `detail_width`; if `left + detail_width < terminal_width` and no child before it grows, the remaining columns stay blank after the right panel.

### Cause B — `size(WIDTH, EQUAL, ...)` is applied after `flex`, cancelling horizontal flex

This is especially suspicious:

```cpp
right | frame | borderRounded | flex | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width)
```

Because outer `size` sets `flex_grow_x = 0`, the panel becomes fixed-width.

### Cause C — `size` is applied before `borderRounded`, so the border makes the panel wider than expected

This:

```cpp
right | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width) | borderRounded
```

means the content is `detail_width`, and the panel is `detail_width + 2`.

If your arithmetic already includes border columns, this can cause off-by-two layout surprises.

---

## Practical fixes

### Fix 1: Make the left pane/filler absorb all extra space before the fixed right pane

```cpp
hbox({
  left | flex,
  right | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width),
})
```

or:

```cpp
hbox({
  left,
  filler(),
  right | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width),
})
```

Use this when the right detail panel should remain a fixed width but be flush with the terminal’s right edge.

---

### Fix 2: If the right detail panel should expand to the edge, put `flex` outside `size`

```cpp
right | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, min_width) | flex
```

This gives it a minimum/equal base width first, then marks it flexible at the outer level.

---

### Fix 3: If `width` is intended to include the border, apply `size` after `borderRounded`

```cpp
right | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, panel_width)
```

If instead `width` is content width, apply `size` before the border:

```cpp
right | frame | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, content_width) | borderRounded
```

---

### Fix 4: Prefer this ordering for scrollable bordered panes

```cpp
content | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, panel_width)
```

or flexible:

```cpp
content | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, min_panel_width) | flex
```

This makes the content scroll inside the border and applies width to the whole decorated panel.

---

## Rule of thumb

For a right detail pane that should touch the far-right edge:

```cpp
hbox({
  left | flex,
  detail | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, detail_width),
})
```

For a right detail pane that should also grow:

```cpp
hbox({
  left | flex,
  detail | frame | borderRounded | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, min_width) | flex,
})
```

Avoid:

```cpp
detail | flex | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, width)
```

because the outer `size` cancels horizontal flex.

