auto& value = direction_ == WIDTH ? requirement_.min_x : requirement_.min_y;

switch (constraint_) {
  case LESS_THAN:
    value = std::min(value, value_);
    break;
  case EQUAL:
    value = value_;
    break;
  case GREATER_THAN:
    value = std::max(value, value_);
    break;
}

if (direction_ == WIDTH) {
  requirement_.flex_grow_x = 0;
  requirement_.flex_shrink_x = 0;
}
```

**Implication**: If the compare pane has `size(WIDTH, ...)` after `flex`, it can stop the pane from expanding horizontally. If you need both, test order carefully:

```cpp
pane | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, n) | flex
```

versus

```cpp
pane | flex | size(WIDTH, EQUAL, n)
```

The latter disables horizontal flex.

